  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Humanitarian Admission Assistance to the State of Berlin in 2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributes to providing a durable solution to 300 beneficiaries of international protection in Lebanon by facilitating their humanitarian admission to Berlin, Germany. This programme is the result of the commitment of the State of Berlin made in 2018 to admit a total of 500 beneficiaries of international protection of mainly Syrian and Iraqi origin residing in Lebanon. Originally, the State set the aim to admit 100 refugees annually over a five-year period. With IOM support, the first two programme cycles were successfully completed in 2021 and 2022 with the overall admission of 213 beneficiaries of international protection. After the German federal and local elections in 2021, the governing parties decided to stabilize and enhance the ongoing state admission programme. For 2022, the State of Berlin therefore pledged to increase the programme and admit 300 beneficiaries of international protection out of Lebanon.</narrative>
  </description>
